# Cursor Cloud specific instructions

These notes apply only to Cursor Cloud agents (kept out of the shared `AGENTS.md` since Vitre is
developed in many places). They cover the VM toolchain and non-obvious run caveats.

## Toolchain

Login shells source `~/.vite-plus/env` from `~/.profile` and `~/.bashrc`. That file prepends
`~/.vite-plus/bin`, where `node` is the Vite+ shim for Node 24.22.2 (`engines.node` is `^24.13.1`)
and `vp` is Vite+ CLI 0.2.2. `vp` is the package manager and task runner (`vp install`, `vp run`,
`vp test`, `vp fmt`) and uses pnpm 11.10.0 (`packageManager`).

- Node gotcha: non-login shells do not source `~/.profile`, so `/exec-daemon` Node 22.23.4 wins on
  `PATH`. Run commands in a login shell (`bash -lc '...'`) or prepend `$HOME/.vite-plus/bin`.
- Rust 1.95.0 with rustfmt and clippy is selected by `rust-toolchain.toml`. Do not `cargo fetch` the
  Zed GPUI git dependency during environment install.
- Native Vitre (`vp run dev:vitre`, `crates/vitre-app`) is macOS-only. Do not build it on these
  Linux VMs.
- `vp check` runs the formatter as well as lint. Format changed markdown with `vp fmt` on those
  files. Do not run repo-wide `vp check`, `vp run typecheck`, or `vp run test` unless asked; CI runs
  the full suite.

## Running the server and marketing site

Cloud agents can run the headless server and the marketing site. The native app cannot run here.

- Headless server, from the repo root:
  `vp run --filter t3 dev -- serve --host 127.0.0.1 --port 3773 --no-browser`.
  It listens on `http://127.0.0.1:3773`. With no static directory and no dev URL, `GET /` returns
  503 and `No static directory configured and no dev URL set.` That response means the process is
  up. Startup also logs a native-app pairing URL.
- Marketing site, from `apps/marketing`:
  `vp exec astro dev --host 127.0.0.1 --port 4173`.
  Root `vp run dev:marketing -- --host` does not forward those flags (Astro treats them as a bad
  command).
- Server state (SQLite, auth, projects) lives under `~/.t3` (`T3CODE_HOME`). Pass `--base-dir <dir>`
  to `serve` or `node apps/server/src/bin.ts project add` to use another directory.
- Agent providers are external CLIs (`codex`, `claude`, `cursor-agent`, `opencode`) probed on
  `PATH`. The server still starts without one. Provider probing runs at startup and refreshes
  roughly every 5 minutes.

## Known flaky tests (unrelated to setup)

- `apps/server/src/git/GitManager.test.ts` (cross-repo PR metadata, can time out at 12s).
- `apps/server/src/provider/Layers/ProviderRegistry.test.ts` (codex binaryPath re-probe ordering).
